# The build context must never contain key material.
#
# data/ IS the wallet: keys.json plus the wallet database, with no
# restore-from-seed behind it. Copying it into an image would publish live
# private keys to every registry and every layer cache the image reaches. This
# repository has already had live keys committed once and purged from history;
# these patterns mirror .gitignore so the same mistake cannot be made through
# the build context instead.
data/
data-*/
*-backup/
*.db
*.db-*
*.key
keys.json
*.tmp

# Not needed to build. Excluding them also keeps the context small, which is
# what lets the go.mod/go.sum layer stay cached across source changes.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
deploy/
*.md
/rule110
/spike
